hadiths[108]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2415","Abdul-Wahhab bin Al-Ward narrated from a man among the inhabitants of Al-Madinah who said:\Mu'awiyah wrote a letter to 'Aishah"""
"2416","Adi bin Hatim narrated that the Messenger of Allah SAW said:\There is no man among you except that his Lord shall converse with him on the Day of Judgement"""
"2417","Ibn Mas'ud narrated that the Messenger of Allah SAW said:\The feet of the son of Adam shall not move from before his Lord on the Day of Judgement"""
"2418","Abu Barzah Al-Aslami narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The feet of the slave of Allah shall not move [on the Day of Judgement] until he is asked about five things: about his life and what he did with it"""
"2419","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Do you know who the bankrupt is?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah SAW! The bankrupt among us is the one who has no Dirham nor property.\"" The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: \""The bankrupt in my Ummah is the one who comes with Salat and fasting and Zakat on the Day of Judgement"""
"2420","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\May Allah have mercy upon a servant who has wronged his brother in his honor or his wealth"""
"2421","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Rights will be given to their due"""
"2422","Narrated by Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The poor will enter Paradise five hundred years before the rich"
"2423","Narrated by Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\The poor among the Muslims will enter Paradise before their wealthy counterparts by half a day"
"2424","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The people will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection bare-foot"""
"2425","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Mani', narrated to us 'Abbad ibn 'Abbad al-Muhalabi, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, who said:\n\nI entered upon 'Aisha رضي الله عنها, and she called for food for me and said, \I have not been filled with food and wished to weep except that I did [weep].\"" He said"
"2426","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The people will face three presentations on the Day of Judgement. As for (the first) two presentations"""
"2427","Ibn 'Abi Mulaikah narrated that 'Aishah said:\I heard the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) saying: 'Whoever his account is questioned about"""
"2428","Anas narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\The son of Adam will be brought on the Day of Judgement as if he is a goat kid to be stood before Allah"""
"2429","Abu Salih reported from Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa'eed that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The servant will be brought on the Day of Judgement"""
"2430","Abu Hurairah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) recited: That Day it will declare its information. And said: 'Do you know what its information is?' they said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'Indeed its information is that it will testify against every servant"""
"2431","Abdullah bin 'Amr bin Al-'As said:\A Bedouin came to the Prophet (S.a.w) and said: 'What is the Sur?' He said: 'A horn that will be blown into'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. It has been reported by more than one narrator from Sulaimãn At-Taimi"""
"2432","Abu Sa'eed narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: 'How can I be comfortable when the one with the horn is holding it to his lip"""
"2433","Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah narrated that The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The sign of the believers upon the Sirat is: O lord"""
"2434","An-Nadr bin Anas bin Malik narrated from his father who said:\I asked the Prophet (s.a.w) to intercede for me on the Day of Judgement. He said: 'I am the one to do so.'\"" [He said:] \""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Then where shall I seek you?' He said: 'Seek me"""
"2435","Abu Hurairah narrated:\\""Some meat was brought to the Prophet (s.a.w) and a foreleg was presented to him"""
"2436","Anas narrated that the Messenger of allah (s.a.w)said:\My intercession is for the people who committed the major sins in my Ummah.\"" Another chain reports a similar narration"""
"2437","# Translation of the Hadith\n\nAl-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us, Ḥaywah ibn Shurayḥ narrated to us, Abū Hānīʾ al-Khawlānī informed me, that Abū ʿAlī ʿAmr ibn Mālik al-Janbī informed him, from Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd رضي الله عنه, that:\n\n**When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in prayer, certain men among them would collapse during the prayer on account of extreme hunger and weakness. These were the Companions of the Ṣuffah (the shaded platform in the Prophet's Mosque). The Bedouins would say of them, \These people are mad\"" or \""These are madmen.\""**\n\n**When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer"
"2438","Abu Umamah narrated the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\My Lord promised me that seventy thousand of my Ummah shall be admitted into Paradise without a reckoning against them nor any punishment. With every thousand"""
"2439","Abdullah bin Shaqiq narrated:\ I was with a troop in Jerusalem"""
"2440","Al-Hasan Al-Basri said:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: 'On the Day of Judgement"""
"2441","Abu Sa'eed narrated the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\Indeed in my Ummah are those who intercede for large groups of people"""
"2442","Abu Al-Malih narrated from 'Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja'i who said:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said 'Someone came to me from my Lord to give me choice between the half of my Ummah being admitted into Paradise or intercession. So I chose the intercession"""
"2443","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed"""
"2444","Samurah narrated the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w)said:\Indeed there is a Hawd for every Prophet"""
"2445","Al-'Abbas narrated from Abu Sallam Al-Habashi who said:\'Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz summoned me so I got a ride on a mule.\"" [He said:] \""When he entered upon him"""
"2446","Abu Dharr narrated:\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What about the vessels of the Hawd?' He said: 'By the one in Whose Hand is my soul! Its vessels number more than the stars of the heavens and the planets on a clear dark night. (They are) among the vessels of Paradise"""
"2447","Ibn 'Abbas narrated :\When the Prophet (s.a.w) was taken for the Night Journey"""
"2448","Abu 'Imaran Al-Jawni narrated :\From Anas bin Malik who said : 'I do not recognize anything (today) from what we were upon during the time of The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w).' So I said : 'What about the Salat?' He said: 'Have you (people) not done what you know (you have done)?'\"" Other chains report similar narrations"""
"2449","Asma bint 'Umais Al-Khath'amiyyah narrated that The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\What an evil servant is the one who fancies himself and becomes vain forgetting the Most Great"""
"2450","Abū ʿĪsā (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīh ḥadīth, gharīb from this chain.\n\nAbū Kurayb narrated to us, Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated to us, from Shaybān, from Firās, from ʿAṭiyyah, from Abū Saʿīd (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever shows off"
"2451","Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us: Haywah ibn Shurayh informed us: al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid Abu 'Uthman al-Madani informed me: 'Uqbah ibn Muslim narrated to him that Shufayy al-Asbahi narrated to him that he entered Madinah and found a man around whom people had gathered. He said: ""Who is this?"" They said: ""Abu Hurayrah."" So I drew near until I sat before him while he was narrating to the people. When he fell silent and was alone, I said to him: ""I adjure you by right and by right to narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that you understood and knew."" Abu Hurayrah said: ""I will do so, to narrate to you a hadith the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me that I understood and knew."" Then Abu Hurayrah had a seizure (nashghah), so he remained a little while, then recovered. He said: ""I will narrate to you a hadith the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me in this house; no one was with us except me and him."" Then Abu Hurayrah had another seizure, then recovered, then wiped his face. He said: ""I will narrate to you a hadith the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me, and I and he were in this house; no one was with us except me and him."" Then Abu Hurayrah had another seizure, then recovered and wiped his face. He said: ""I will do so, to narrate to you a hadith the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me, and I was with him in this house; no one was with him except me and him."" Then Abu Hurayrah had a severe seizure, then fell prostrate on his face. I supported him against me for a long while, then he recovered. He said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, when it is the Day of Resurrection, will descend to the servants to judge between them, and every nation will be kneeling. The first to be called will be a man who memorized the Qur'an, a man who was killed in the path of Allah, and a man of abundant wealth. Allah will say to the reciter: 'Did I not teach you what I sent down upon My Messenger?' He will say: 'Yes, O Lord.' He will say: 'What did you do with what you were taught?' He will say: 'I used to stand with it (recite it) in the watches of the night and the watches of the day.' Allah will say to him: 'You lied.' And the angels will say to him: 'You lied.' And Allah will say to him: 'Rather, you wanted it to be said: So-and-so is a reciter.' So it was said. Then the man of wealth will be brought. Allah will say to him: 'Did I not expand for you so that you had no need of anyone?' He will say: 'Yes, O Lord.' He will say: 'What did you do with what I gave you?' He will say: 'I used to maintain ties of kinship and give charity.' Allah will say to him: 'You lied.' And the angels will say to him: 'You lied.' And Allah, Exalted, will say: 'Rather, you wanted it to be said: So-and-so is generous.' So it was said. Then the one killed in the path of Allah will be brought. Allah will say to him: 'In what were you killed?' He will say: 'I was commanded to fight in Your path, so I fought until I was killed.' Allah, Exalted, will say to him: 'You lied.' And the angels will say to him: 'You lied.' And Allah will say: 'Rather, you wanted it to be said: So-and-so is brave.' So it was said."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck my knee and said: ""O Abu Hurayrah, those three are the first of Allah's creation with whom the Fire will be kindled on the Day of Resurrection."" Al-Walid Abu 'Uthman said: 'Uqbah ibn Muslim informed me that Shufayy is the one who entered upon Mu'awiyah and informed him of this. Abu 'Uthman said: Al-'Ala' ibn Abi Hakim narrated to me that he was Mu'awiyah's executioner. A man entered upon him and informed him of this from Abu Hurayrah. Mu'awiyah said: ""This has been done to these people; then how about the rest of the people?"" Then Mu'awiyah wept intensely until we thought he would perish. We said: ""This man has brought us evil."" Then Mu'awiyah recovered and wiped his face and said: ""Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth: 'Whoever desires the life of this world and its adornment, We will fully repay them for their deeds therein, and they therein will not be deprived. Those are the ones for whom there is nothing in the Hereafter but the Fire. And lost is what they did therein, and worthless is what they used to do' (11:15-16)."" Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan gharib hadith."
"2452","Rabi'ah bin Yazid and 'Atiyyah bin Qais narrated from 'Atiyyah As-Sa'di - and he was one of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) - that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\The servant shall not reach the state of being among the Muttaqin until he leaves what there is no harm in out of caution for its harm"""
"2453","Hanzalah Al-Usaiyyidi narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\If you would (always) be as you are with me"""
"2454","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Indeed for everything there is a zeal"""
"2455","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated \The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) drew a square line (on the ground) forus"""
"2456","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w)said:\The son of Adam grows old. But two things keep him young: Desire for life and desire for wealth"""
"2457","Mutarrif bin 'Abdullah bin Ash-Shikh-khir narrated from his father from the Prophet(s.a.w) who said:\The case of the son of Adam is such that he is surrounded by ninety-nine calamities"""
"2458","At-Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka'b narrated from his father who said:\When a third of the night had passed"""
"2459","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\ Have Haya' for Allah as is His due.\"" [He said:] We said: \""O Prophet of Allah! We have Haya'"""
"2460","Shaddad bin Aws narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\The clever person ids the one who subjugates his soul"""
"2461","Abu Sa'eed narrated:\ The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) entered his Musalla and saw the people who looked as if they were smiling. So he said: 'Indeed"""
"2462","It was narrated to us by Hannād and Qutaybahah, who both said: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl related to us from ʿImrān ibn Muslim al-Qaṣīr, from Saʿīd ibn Salmān, from Yazīd ibn Nuʿāmah al-Ḍabbī, who stated:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n**\When a man establishes a bond of brotherhood with another man"
"2463","Al-Mustawrad bin Makhramah narrated that 'Amir bin 'Awf informed him- and he was an ally of Banu 'Amr bin Lu'ay who had participated with The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) at(the battle of ) Badr"
"2464","Urwah bin Az-Zubair and Ibn Musayyab narrated that Hakim bin Hizam said:\I (once) asked the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) (for something) and he gave it to me. Then I asked him (again) and he gave it to me. Then I asked him (again) and he gave it to me. Then I asked him (again)"""
"2465","Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf said:\We were tested along with the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) by adversity"""
"2466","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\Whoever makes the Hereafter his goal"""
"2467","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\Indeed Allah"""
"2468","Aishah said :\ The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) died and we had a Shatr of barley. We ate from it as Allah willed"""
"2469","Aishah narrated:\We had a cloth which had some pictures on it as a curtain on my door. The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) saw it and said: 'Remove it"""
"2470","Aishah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) had a leather cushion stuffed with palm fibres which he would lean on"""
"2471","Abu Maisarah narrated from 'Aishah that they had slaughtered a sheep"
"2472","Narrated by Muḥammad ibn Ḥumayd al-Rāzī and Yūsuf ibn Mūsā al-Qaṭṭān al-Baghdādī, who both said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Maghrāʾ, Abū Zuhayr, narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n> \The people of well-being (ahl al-ʿāfiyah) will wish on the Day of Resurrection"
"2473","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed I have feared for the sake of Allah"""
"2474","Muhammad bin Ka'b Al-Qurazi said:\Someone narrated to me that he heard 'ali bin abi Talib saying: 'I went out on a cold day from the house of the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w). I had taken a tanned skin"""
"2475","Abu 'Uthman An-Nahdi narrated from Abu Hurairah that they (the Companions) were suffering from hunger so the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) gave them each a date"
"2476","Jabir bin 'Abdullah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) dispatched us"""
"2477","Yazid bin Ziyad narrated from Muhammad bin Ka'b Al-Qurazi who heard from Abi Talib narrated that he said:'I was sitting in a gathering with the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) when Mus'ab bin 'Umair appeared before us"
"2478","Abu Hurairah narrated:\The people of As-Suffah were the guests of the people of Islam"""
"2479","Yahya Al-Bakka' narrated from Ibn 'Umar who said:\A man belched in the presence of the Prophet(s.a.w)"""
"2480","Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa narrated that his father said:\O my son! If you saw us when we were with the Prophet(s.a.w) and the sky poured upon us"""
"2481","It was narrated to us by Abu ‘Abdullah, Muhammad ibn Abi Thalgh al-Baghdadi, the companion of Ahmad ibn Hanbal. It was narrated to us by ‘Ali ibn Hafs, who said: It was narrated to us by Ibrahim ibn ‘Abdullah ibn Hatim, from ‘Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\Do not talk much without the remembrance of Allah"
"2482","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and others narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays al-Makki narrated to us, saying: I heard Sa'id ibn Hassan al-Makhzumi say: Umm Salih narrated to me, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\All the speech of the son of Adam is against him"
"2483","Shahib bin Bashir narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\All expenditures are in Allah's Cause"""
"2484","Harithah bin Mudarrib said:\We went to visit Khabbab who had himself cauterized in seven places on his body. He said: 'I have been ill for so long"""
"2485","Abdullah bin Salam said:\When the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) arrived- meaning in Al-Madinah – the people came out to meet him. It was said that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) had arrived"""
"2486","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\The one who eats and is grateful is like the status of the patient fasting person"""
"2487","Anas said:\When the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) arrived in Al-Madinah the Muhajirun came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! We have not seen a people more willing to sacrifice when having a lot"""
"2488","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Shall I not inform you of whom the Fire is unlawful and he is unlawful for the Fire? Every person who is near (to people)"""
"2489","Aswad bin Yazid narrated:\I said to Aishah: 'What would the Prophet (s.a.w) do when he entered his house?' She said: 'He would busy himself with serving his family"""
"2490","Anas bin Malik narrated:\When the Prophet(s.a.w) would receive a man to shake hands with him"""
"2491","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\A man among those before you went out arrogantly in a Hullah of his. So Allah ordered the earth to take him. He remains sinking[into it]\"" - or he said - \""He will remain sinking into it until the Day of Judgement"""
"2492","Abū Zakariyyā, Yaḥyā ibn Durust al-Baṣrī, narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd reported to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said — and Ḥammād added that, according to them, it is marfūʿ (elevated to the Prophet ﷺ) — regarding the verse: **\The Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds\""** (Qurʾān 83:6)"
"2493","It was narrated to us by Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān, who narrated to us from Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī, who narrated to us from Sufyān, from al-Mughīrah ibn al-Nuʿmān, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\On the Day of Resurrection"
"2494","Abu Bakr bin Al-Munkadir narrated from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\There are three (characteristics) for which whomever has them"""
"2495","Abu Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""Allah,Most High said: 'O My Slaves! All of you are astray except whom I guide, so ask Me for guidance and I shall guide you. All of you are poor except whom I enrich, so ask Me and I shall provide you. All of you are sinners except whom I have pardoned, so whoever among you knows that I am the One able to forgive, and seeks My forgiveness, I shall forgive him, without concern for Me (and it will not affect Me). If the first of you and the last of you, the living among you and the dead among you, the fresh among you and the dry among you were to gather together to help the heart with the most Taqwa among My slaves, that would not add a mosquito's wing to My sovereignty. If the first of you and the last of you, the living among you and the dead among you, the fresh among you and the dry among you were to gather together to help the worst heart of My slaves, that would not diminish a mosquito's wing to My sovereignty. I shall forgive him, without concern for Me (and it will not affect Me). If the first of you and the last of you, the living among you and the dead among you, the fresh among you and the dry among you were to gather together upon one plateau, and each person among them were to ask for his utmost desire, and I were to give each what he asked for, that would not diminish from My sovereignty, except as if one of you were to pass by an ocean and dip a needle into it and then remove it. That is because I am the Most Liberal without need, the Most Generous, doing as I will. I give by My speech and I punish by My speech, whenever I will something I only say: ""Be"" and it shall be.'"" Another chain reports a similar narration"
"2496","Ibn 'Umar said:\I heard the Prophet (s.a.w) narrating a hadith"""
"2497","Al-Harith bin Suwaid said:"" 'Abdullah [bin Mas'ud] narrated two Ahadith to us, one of them from himself and the other from the Prophet (s.a.w). 'Abdullah said: 'The believer sees his sins as if he was at the base of a mountain, fearing that it was about to fall upon him. The wicked person sees his sins as if (they are) flies are hitting his nose"" he said: ""Like this"" - motioning with his hand - ""to get them to fly away"
"2498","And the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Allah is more pleased with the repentance of one of you that a man in a desolate"""
"2499","Anas narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\Every son of Adam sins"""
"2500","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"""
"2501","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Whoever is silent"""
"2502","Abu Hudhaifah narrated - and he was one of the companions of 'Abdullãh bin Mas'üd - from 'Aishah who said:\I told the Prophet (ﷺ) about a man"""
"2503","Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\I do not like to talk about anyone"""
"2504","Suwayd ibn Nasr informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Abū Ḥayyān al-Taymī informed us, from Abū Zurʿah ibn ʿAmr ibn Jarīr, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought some meat, and the forearm was presented to him. He ate from it, and it was a piece he liked. He took a bite from it, then said: ""I am the master of the people on the Day of Resurrection. Do you know why that is? Allah will gather the first and the last of mankind on a single plain. A caller will make them hear, and the sight will penetrate them, and the sun will draw near to them. The people will experience such distress and anguish that they cannot bear or endure. The people will say to one another: 'Do you not see what has befallen you? Will you not look for someone to intercede for you with your Lord?' The people will say to one another: 'Go to Adam.' They will come to Adam and say: 'You are the father of mankind. Allah created you with His Hand, breathed into you from His Spirit, and commanded the angels to prostrate to you. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in? Do you not see what has befallen us?' Adam will say to them: 'My Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been angry before, nor will He ever be angry like it again. He forbade me from the tree, but I disobeyed. Myself, myself, myself! Go to someone else; go to Nūḥ.' They will come to Nūḥ and say: 'O Nūḥ, you are the first of the Messengers to the people of the earth, and Allah has named you a grateful servant. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in? Do you not see what has befallen us?' Nūḥ will say: 'My Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been angry before, nor will He ever be angry like it again. I had a supplication which I made against my people. Myself, myself, myself! Go to someone else; go to Ibrāhīm.' They will come to Ibrāhīm and say: 'O Ibrāhīm, you are the Prophet of Allah and His intimate friend (Khalīl) among the people of the earth. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in?' He will say: 'My Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been angry before, nor will He ever be angry like it again. I told three lies.' Abū Ḥayyān mentioned them in the hadith. 'Myself, myself, myself! Go to someone else; go to Mūsā.' They will come to Mūsā and say: 'O Mūsā, you are the Messenger of Allah. Allah favored you with His Message and His Speech above mankind. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in?' He will say: 'My Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been angry before, nor will He ever be angry like it again. I killed a soul I was not commanded to kill. Myself, myself, myself! Go to someone else; go to ʿĪsā.' They will come to ʿĪsā and say: 'O ʿĪsā, you are the Messenger of Allah and His Word which He cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Him. You spoke to the people in the cradle. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in?' ʿĪsā will say: 'My Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been angry before, nor will He ever be angry like it again.' He did not mention a sin. 'Myself, myself, myself! Go to someone else; go to Muḥammad.' They will come to Muḥammad and say: 'O Muḥammad, you are the Messenger of Allah and the Seal of the Prophets. Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in?' So I will set out and come beneath the Throne, then fall prostrate before my Lord. Then Allah will reveal to me some of His praises and good commendation such as He has never revealed to anyone before me. Then it will be said: 'O Muḥammad, raise your head. Ask, and you shall be given. Intercede, and your intercession shall be accepted.' I will raise my head and say: 'O Lord, my Ummah! O Lord, my Ummah! O Lord, my Ummah!' It will be said: 'O Muḥammad, admit those of your Ummah who have no account to give through the right-hand gate of Paradise. They will be partners with the people in the other gates.' Then he said: 'By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the distance between the two leaves of the gates of Paradise is like the distance between Makkah and Hajar, or like the distance between Makkah and Busrā.'"" And in this chapter there are narrations from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, Anas, ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, and Abū Saʿīd. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth. Abū Ḥayyān al-Taymī's name is Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd ibn Ḥayyān, a Kūfan, and he is trustworthy. Abū Zurʿah ibn ʿAmr ibn Jarīr's name is Harim."
"2505","Khalid bin Ma'dan narrated from Mu'adh bin Jabal that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Whoever shames his brother for a sin"""
"2506","Wathilah bin Al-Asqa' narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Do not rejoice over the mishaps of your brother so that Allah has mercy on him and subjects you to trials"""
"2507","Yahya bin Wath-thab narrated:\From a Shaikh among the Companions of the Prophet (s.a.w)"""
"2508","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Beware of evil with each other"""
"2509","Abu Ad-Darda' narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Shall I not inform you of what is more virtuous than the rank of fasting"""
"2510","Az-Zubair bin Al-'Awwam narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\The disease of the nations before you is creeping towards you: Envy and hatred"""
"2511","Abu Bakrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\There is no sin more worthy of Allah hastening the punishment upon its practitioner in the world – along with what is in store for him in the Hereafter – than tyranny and severing the ties of kinship.” (Sahih)"""
"2512","Amr bin Shu'aib narrated from his grandfather 'Abdullah bin 'Amr"
"2513","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Look to one who is lower than you"""
"2514","Abu 'Uthman narrated from Hanzalah Al-Usaidi – and he was one of the scribes of the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w)- that he passed by Abu Bakr while he was crying"
"2515","Anas narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself"""
"2516","Ibn 'Abbas narrated:\I was behind the Prophet(s.a.w) one day when he said: 'O boy! I will teach you a statement: Be mindful of Allah and He will protect you. Be mindful of Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask"""
"2517","Anas bin Malik narrated that a man said:\O Messenger of Allah! Shall I tie it and rely(upon Allah)"""
"2518","Al-Hasan bin 'Ali said:\I remember that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: 'Leave what makes you in doubt for what does not make you in doubt. The truth brings tranquility while falsehood sows doubt.'\"" Another chain reports a similar narration"""
"2519","Narrated by Abū Sa‘īd al-Khudri (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n“Whosoever believer feeds a hungry believer, Allāh will feed him on the Day of Resurrection from the fruits of Paradise. And whosoever believer gives drink to a thirsty believer, Allāh will give him to drink on the Day of Resurrection from the sealed nectar (al-Rahīq al-Makhtūm). And whosoever believer clothes a naked believer, Allāh will clothe him from the green garments of Paradise.”\n\nAbū ‘Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This hadīth is gharīb (uncommon). It has also been narrated from ‘Aṭiyyah from Abū Sa‘īd as a mawqūf (a statement attributed only to the Companion), and that is more correct and more likely according to us."
"2520","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Whoever eats the Tayyib and acts in accordance with the Sunnah"""
"2521","Sahl bin Mu'adh[bin Anas] Al-Juhni narrated from his father that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Whoever gives for the sake of Allah"""
"2522","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\The first batch to enter Paradise will appear like the moon of a night that is full. The second will appear like the color of the most beautiful star in the sky. Each man among them shall have two wives"""
